# Walkthrough - Fixing Login/Registration Internal Server Error

I have resolved the issue where users were experiencing a `500 Internal Server Error` when registering or logging in with passwords longer than 72 characters. This was due to a limitation in the `bcrypt` hashing library, which the backend now handles gracefully with validation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Password Length Validation
I resolved the issue where passwords longer than 72 characters caused a crash in the `bcrypt` library.
- **[auth.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/auth.py)**: Added validation to the registration, login, and profile update endpoints to return a clean error instead of crashing.
- **[user.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/user.py)**: Added a safety check in the [User](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/user.py#14-48) model as a last line of defense.

### 3. Password Reset Functionality
I've added a complete password reset flow to allow users to recover their accounts.
-   **Model**: Added [PasswordResetToken](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/password_reset_token.py#15-30) to track secure, time-limited reset tokens.
-   **Backend**: Added `/forgot-password` (token generation) and `/reset-password` (password update) endpoints to [auth.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/auth.py).
-   **Frontend**: Created dedicated pages for requesting resets and setting new passwords, and added a "Forgot Password?" link to the login screen.
-   **Timezone Consistency**: Ensured all token expiration checks use the Singapore timezone (Asia/Singapore) to match the rest of the system.

